description:
In the Kanban board, when filtering we can only type one letter at a time because the filter input loses focus on every keystroke.

## Symptoms
1. Click on the filter/search input in Kanban board
2. Type a letter
3. Input immediately loses focus
4. Must click again to type the next letter
5. Very frustrating UX - practically unusable

## Root Cause Analysis
The filter input likely triggers a re-render of the component on every keystroke, which causes:
1. The input element to be recreated
2. Focus to be lost
3. User cannot type continuously

## Suggested Fix
1. **Don't re-render on filter change** - Only update the filtered results, not the input itself
2. **Add debounce** - Wait 200-300ms after last keystroke before processing filter
3. **Preserve focus** - After any re-render, restore focus to the filter input
4. **Use controlled input** - Manage input value in state without re-rendering the input element

## Implementation Notes
```javascript
// Option 1: Debounce the filter
let filterTimeout;
input.addEventListener('input', (e) => {
    clearTimeout(filterTimeout);
    filterTimeout = setTimeout(() => {
        this.filterCards(e.target.value);
    }, 250);
});

// Option 2: Only update card visibility, not the whole render
filterCards(term) {
    this.querySelectorAll('.kb-card').forEach(card => {
        card.style.display = card.textContent.includes(term) ? '' : 'none';
    });
}
```

## Priority
High - severely impacts usability of Kanban board
